What is the difference between IActionResult, ActionResult, and ActionResult<T> in .NET Core?

First learn this simple example:
[HttpGet]
public IActionResult GetEmployee()
{
    return Ok("Employee found");
}


- IActionResult → Returns different HTTP responses like Ok(), NotFound(), BadRequest().
- ActionResult<T> → Returns a specific data type or an HTTP response.
- ActionResult → Base class for action results.
